---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "astro-theme-university/url";
import heroImage from "../assets/images/hero-home.svg";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";

const lectures = (await getCollection("lectures")).sort((a, b) => a.data.week - b.data.week);

const blocks = [...new Map(lectures.map((lecture) => [lecture.data.block, lecture.data.blockTitle])).entries()]
  .sort(([a], [b]) => Number(a) - Number(b))
  .map(([block, blockTitle]) => {
    const weeks = lectures.filter((lecture) => lecture.data.block === block);
    return {
      block,
      blockTitle,
      firstWeek: weeks[0].data.week,
      lastWeek: weeks[weeks.length - 1].data.week,
    };
  });
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  heroImage={heroImage}
  heroImageAlt="A grid of envelopes in flat black and gold, most sealed and face-down at slightly uneven angles, two turned face-up and opened, in a two-ink risograph print"
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <p>This course is more informally known as "Nobody Owes You a Reply".</p>

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    Twelve weeks, each built around one specific way a cold email fails:
    a vague ask, a subject line that hides its own point, a follow-up that
    costs the reader twice for nothing. Each week's Weekly Sync puts that
    week's idea to work on a real email, so the practice keeps pace with
    the teaching. A midterm teardown asks you to find ten problems
    yourself, with no lecture pointing you to them, and the semester ends
    with a one-page personal doctrine on what makes an email worth
    sending, defended against one you'd actually send yourself.
  </p>

  <h2>Course structure</h2>
  <p>
    Runs in Semester 1, 2027 only. No prerequisites. Each week
    pairs a one-hour lecture (Mondays, 11am–12pm, Sloppy Slop Slop Building,
    Rm 7.09) with a one-hour Weekly Sync, for two contact hours a week.
    Graded CRS (pass/fail); it does not count toward GPA.
  </p>
  <table class="block-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Block</th>
        <th scope="col">Theme</th>
        <th scope="col">Weeks</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {
        blocks.map((b) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{b.block}</td>
            <td>{b.blockTitle}</td>
            <td>{b.firstWeek}–{b.lastWeek}</td>
          </tr>
        ))
      }
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    There are three assessments. See the <a href={withBase("/assessments/")}>assessment
    page</a> for the brief and due dates of each.
  </p>

  <h3>Weekly Sync timetable</h3>
  <p>Each Weekly Sync is run by one of the three tutors:</p>
  <p>
    Weekly Syncs work like tutorials: attendance is mandatory and required
    to pass the course. The exercises done in each sync build directly on
    that week's lecture and feed into the assessments, so keeping up with
    them is critical to doing well.
  </p>
  <table class="sync-timetable">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Tutor</th>
        <th scope="col">Day</th>
        <th scope="col">Time</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={withBase("/people/tucker-vance/")}>Tucker Vance</a></td>
        <td>Tuesday</td>
        <td>2pm–3pm</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={withBase("/people/oliver-bennett/")}>Oliver Bennett</a></td>
        <td>Wednesday</td>
        <td>10am–11am</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={withBase("/people/wei-chen/")}>Wei Chen</a></td>
        <td>Thursday</td>
        <td>4pm–5pm</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    If you have a question, email <a href="mailto:SLOP3089@slop.university">SLOP3089@slop.university</a>{" "}
    or use the Canvas page.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone who has to get a stranger to read something and reply: founders
    doing outbound, students emailing for a reference or a chance at a role,
    anyone tired of writing "I hope this finds you well" and meaning none of
    it. No prior coursework is assumed. What's assumed is that you've sent an
    email that never got a reply and would like to know why.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title="Lectures" href="/lectures/">
      <p>The full teaching content, week by week.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>The tutor-led hour and exercises attached to each week's lecture.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>What is marked, what it is worth, and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Policies" href="/policies/">
      <p>Extensions, academic integrity and the rest of the fine print.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Students' Union" href="mailto:sa.union@slop.university">
      <p>
        Independent help with academic integrity issues and anything you'd
        rather not raise with us directly.
      </p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .block-table,
  .sync-timetable {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-block: 1rem 2rem;
    table-layout: auto;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .block-table th,
  .block-table td,
  .sync-timetable th,
  .sync-timetable td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--at-border, #d0d0d0);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
</style>
